sentences.l:
But yet the same once to the chariot to submit accustomed
four-footed creatures, and bridles to the yoke in harmony to bear;
hope also of peace,” he says.

sentences.t:
Tum numina sancta precamur
Palladis armisonae, quae prima accepit ovantis,
et capita ante aras Phrygio velamur amictu;

sentences.l:
Then the divine powers holy we pray to
of Pallas of the clashing arms, who first received us rejoicing,
and our heads before the altars we cover with the Phrygian robe;

sentences.t:
interdumque atram prorumpit ad aethera nubem,
turbine fumantem piceo et candente favilla,
attollitque globos flammarum et sidera lambit;

sentences.l:
and at times a black cloud it bursts out to the upper air,
smoking with a pitchy whirlwind and glowing ash,
and lifts balls of flames and the stars licks;

sentences.t:
Fama est Enceladi semustum fulmine corpus
urgueri mole hac, ingentemque insuper Aetnam
impositam ruptis flammam exspirare caminis;

sentences.l:
There is a story that Enceladus's half-burnt body by the thunderbolt
is pressed down by this mass, and huge above it Etna
laid on it, from the broken furnaces breathes out flame;

sentences.t:
Isque ubi Dardanios habitus et Troia vidit
arma procul, paulum aspectu conterritus haesit,
continuitque gradum;

sentences.l:
And he, when the Dardanian dress and the Trojan
arms from afar he saw, a little at the sight terrified stopped,
and checked his step;

sentences.t:
“Per sidera testor,
per superos atque hoc caeli spirabile lumen,
tollite me, Teucri;

sentences.l:
“By the stars I call witness,
by the gods above and by this breathable light of heaven,
